  "description": "YILRAQ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H104 Dy9 N6 O52 1+,C2 H3 O2 1-,16(H2 O1),3(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.551-5.036 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.10-153.95°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy9(S-Hftp)(S-H2btp)2(OAc)6(μ3-OH)10(H2O)6](OAc)·solvents. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 10 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 10 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
